# pip-audit ignore list
#
# Format: one vulnerability ID per line. Each entry MUST have a "# reason:"
# comment immediately above explaining why the risk is accepted.
#
# Adding to this file is the LAST resort. First try:
#   1. Upgrade the affected package
#   2. Switch to a different package
#   3. Pin a floor version that contains the fix
# Only use --ignore-vuln when the upstream has no fix available
# and the vulnerability is not exploitable in our usage pattern.
#
# Every entry below was verified to FIRE in a clean project venv built from
# requirements.lock; audit that environment. An entry that stops
# firing is dead and must be deleted rather than left to rot. Do not add an
# entry from a scan of an ambient environment: audit a clean venv built from
# the lock, otherwise advisories for packages the project does not ship end up
# suppressed.

# Do not re-add suppressions for torch, starlette or cryptography advisories
# without a clean-venv scan that shows them firing: the locked versions of
# those packages are outside the affected ranges.

# No entries. PYSEC-2026-597 (nltk downloader path traversal) was removed: a
# scan of a clean venv built from requirements.lock no longer reports it.
